{"name":"Cobbler","hex":"#c4ab7d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cobbler","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person from Northamptonshire (traditionally a centre for shoemaking)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cobbler"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shoemaking","blocks":[{"text":"Shoemaking is the process of making footwear."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Schuhmacher-1568.png/330px-Schuhmacher-1568.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoemaking"},{"title":"Cobbler (food)","blocks":[{"text":"Cobbler is a dessert or savory dish consisting of a fruit or savoury filling poured into a large baking dish and covered with a batter, biscuit, or dumpling before being baked. Cobbler is part of the cuisine of the United Kingdom, Australia and United States. The Joy of Cooking said of the cobbler, \"while neither tidy or shapely, it is indisputably delicious\", while The Washington Post said the phrase \"as American as apple pie\" should really be \"as American as a cobbler\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Cobbler_%287303683612%29.jpg/330px-Cobbler_%287303683612%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cobbler_(food)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/10_peintures_annamites_repr%C3%A9sentant_les_m%C3%A9tiers_au_Tonkin_%28%22La_cordonni%C3%A8re%22%29.jpg/500px-10_peintures_annamites_repr%C3%A9sentant_les_m%C3%A9tiers_au_Tonkin_%28%22La_cordonni%C3%A8re%22%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/10_peintures_annamites_repr%C3%A9sentant_les_m%C3%A9tiers_au_Tonkin_%28%22La_cordonni%C3%A8re%22%29.jpg/500px-10_peintures_annamites_repr%C3%A9sentant_les_m%C3%A9tiers_au_To